{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01475",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.27,
      "end_seconds": 4.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Hello, sorry about the delay, do sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.66,
      "end_seconds": 12.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Uh, hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.42,
      "end_seconds": 16.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.1,
      "end_seconds": 25.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "I mean, uh, I'm here because of wheezing when I exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.32,
      "end_seconds": 33.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.02,
      "end_seconds": 40.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.25,
      "end_seconds": 44.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Mm, okay. What aggravates it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.09,
      "end_seconds": 51.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Let me think, cold air and running definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.45,
      "end_seconds": 55.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.13,
      "end_seconds": 66.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.87,
      "text": "It's, It's every other day. And, And there's a cough at night as well, two months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.98,
      "end_seconds": 74.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Have you had wheezing when you exercise before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.29,
      "end_seconds": 81.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.68,
      "end_seconds": 84.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.12,
      "end_seconds": 94.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.09,
      "end_seconds": 119.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.14,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 98 percent, respiratory rate 15, BP is 126 over 76. And pulse is 84 beats a minute, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.03,
      "end_seconds": 121.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.39,
      "end_seconds": 126.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.21,
      "end_seconds": 132.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "So, I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.87,
      "end_seconds": 136.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.92,
      "end_seconds": 155.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "I can hear a faint wheeze at the end of breathing out, otherwise the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.53,
      "end_seconds": 166.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "You can sit up now. And what about ankle swelling, fever, chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.24,
      "end_seconds": 170.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.0,
      "end_seconds": 173.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.04,
      "end_seconds": 179.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Um, you know, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.44,
      "end_seconds": 183.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.59,
      "end_seconds": 188.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.05,
      "end_seconds": 205.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.16,
      "end_seconds": 211.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Right, um, no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.94,
      "end_seconds": 229.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.16,
      "end_seconds": 236.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Right, I take Seretide inhaler, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.26,
      "end_seconds": 253.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.32,
      "end_seconds": 260.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Just a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.69,
      "end_seconds": 265.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.23,
      "end_seconds": 267.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "I've got asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.8,
      "end_seconds": 275.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Okay, I can see asthma in your file as well. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.95,
      "end_seconds": 296.35,
      "duration_seconds": 15.4,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I live with my elderly mother. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.2,
      "end_seconds": 329.35,
      "duration_seconds": 32.15,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, it points towards exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy. Another possibility is a viral chest infection. Let's get a peak flow diary, for asthma. I'm going to order an allergy test, for seasonal symptoms. Let's use budesonide-formoterol inhaler, 200 micrograms, one puff twice a day, long term. That should help with asthma control. Rinse your mouth after the preventer inhaler and use the spacer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.88,
      "end_seconds": 343.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.79,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: the inhaler isn't helping or you cannot speak in full sentences. In that case don't wait. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.69,
      "end_seconds": 353.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Hmm, good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}